text.en:
There may be paid into a client account —

(a) trust money;

(b) such money belonging to the advocate and solicitor as may be necessary for the purpose of opening or maintaining the account;

(c) money to replace any such which may by mistake or accident have been drawn from the account in contravention of rule 8(2); and

(d) a cheque or draft received by the advocate and solicitor, which under rule 5 he is entitled to split but which he does not split.
